Ventilation



Your home currently has various components that contribute to ventilation:

        - the kitchen range hood fan vents to the outside

        - there are 2 bathroom fans that vents to the outside

        - there is a clothes dryer that exhausts to the exterior

        - there is a 4" fresh air supply pipe connected to the furnace ductwork

        - there is a 6" combustion air pipe in the mechanical room that I think is acting as both a combustion air supply

          for the hot water tank &amp; also as additional make-up air supply for the exhaust fans outlined above



You may want to consider installing bathroom fan timer switches (where you select 5, 10, 15, 20 minutes) so these fans can remain on for an adequate time to remove bathroom moisture and/or odours without the risk of being left on all day and wasting heat.



In the ventilation section of this report, I modeled the option to install a Heat Recovery Ventilation (HRV) system.



-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------



Depressurization Test



The result of the exhaust devices depressurization test, which consists of turning on all exhaust equipment (range hood fan, bathroom fan, but not the dryer as it was not yet installed), indicated a pressure drop of 26.0 Pascals. As this number is higher than 5 Pascals, the use of this equipment can cause combustion products to be drawn into your home, if you have any chimney vented appliances in your home that are not direct-vent. Your current furnace is direct vent, the wood fireplace has been decommissioned &amp; the hot water tank is power vented (with a combustion air supply pipe in the mechanical room) so there is little chance of back-drafting combustion gases from the hot water tank into your house.



During my assessment of your home, there appeared to be functioning smoke and carbon monoxide (CO) detectors. Please ensure both types of detectors are always installed &amp; operational in your home, and not beyond their "replace by" date.



